Sweep finding from #22, unrelated to the leak but on the same error paths.

Crypt/Age.pm:108, 111, 155, 158 use bare "die" for the in-memory filehandle opens:

  open my $ifh, :raw, \$plaintext or die "open on input string: $!";

getty-perl-core is explicit that croak is the house rule and die where croak belongs is forbidden -- these report Crypt/Age.pm as the origin instead of the caller. They interpolate only $! so they are not a leak; every other error path in the file already croaks. Four one-word changes.

Worth pairing with #20, which is about coverage of the documented error paths: the message text changes (croak appends the caller location instead of ours), so it is a user-visible change and wants its own Changes line.

Also noticed on the same path and not ticketed separately: an undef entry in the recipients array produces two "Use of uninitialized value" warnings from Header::create before the croak. Argument validation is its own concern -- recording it here so it is not rediscovered.
